  "narrative": {
    "intro": "This page ranks federal contracts whose period of performance ends within the next 12 months and highlights upcoming recompete opportunities. The list of expiring contracts totals $316B in award value across all entries. NATIONAL TECHNOLOGY & ENGINEERING SOLUTIONS OF SANDIA, LLC has the single largest expiring contract at $43.5B, followed by CONSOLIDATED NUCLEAR SECURITY, LLC at $34.7B and multiple entries for THE BOEING COMPANY at $32B, $18.1B, and $7.5B. The expiring contract value breaks down by quarter: Oct-Dec 2026 at $37.6B, Jan-Mar 2027 at $45.5B, Apr-Jun 2027 at $82.5B, Jul-Sep 2027 at $151B, and Oct-Dec 2027 at $0. Award value figures are total contract values for contracts whose period of performance ends within the next 12 months. End dates can be extended by options and modifications. This view highlights where large recompetes will be concentrated so companies can prioritize capture and teaming efforts around the named contractors and the quarters with the largest expirations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which contractors hold the largest expiring contracts and when do those contracts end?",
        "body": "NATIONAL TECHNOLOGY & ENGINEERING SOLUTIONS OF SANDIA, LLC holds an expiring contract valued at $43.5B. CONSOLIDATED NUCLEAR SECURITY, LLC holds an expiring contract valued at $34.7B. THE BOEING COMPANY holds expiring contracts valued at $32B, $18.1B, and $7.5B, and the quarter with the largest aggregate expirations is Jul-Sep 2027 at $151B."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How are expiring contract values distributed across the coming quarters?",
        "body": "Oct-Dec 2026 accounts for $37.6B in expiring value and Jan-Mar 2027 accounts for $45.5B. Apr-Jun 2027 accounts for $82.5B and Jul-Sep 2027 accounts for $151B. Oct-Dec 2027 shows $0 in expiring contract value."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "Which large federal contracts are expiring soon?",
      "a": "Large federal contracts expiring soon include NATIONAL TECHNOLOGY & ENGINEERING SOLUTIONS OF SANDIA, LLC ($43.5B), CONSOLIDATED NUCLEAR SECURITY, LLC ($34.7B), THE BOEING COMPANY ($32B, $18.1B, $7.5B), SAVANNAH RIVER NUCLEAR SOLUTIONS LLC ($27.6B), LOCKHEED MARTIN SERVICES, LLC ($20.6B), ELECTRIC BOAT CORPORATION ($20.4B), BELL BOEING JOINT PROJECT OFFICE ($7B), and CHEMONICS INTERNATIONAL, INC. ($6.7B)."
