    {
      "q": "What is a contract recompete?",
      "a": "A contract recompete is the process the government uses to solicit new proposals and award a successor contract when an existing contract's period of performance ends, allowing the agency to select a new or incumbent contractor for continued work."
    },
    {
      "q": "How current is this recompete data?",
      "a": "This recompete data covers FY2027 to date, and award value figures represent total contract values for contracts whose period of performance ends within the next 12 months; end dates can be extended by options and modifications."
